iv class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="user" data-message-id="db4d3070-15e9-4484-af1b-2ca016f1fa5f" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden items-end rtl:items-start"><div class="flex gap-2 flex-wrap mt-1 max-w-[80%] justify-end"><div class="relative flex group/file-tile text-token-text-primary relative inline-flex w-(--file-tile-width) min-w-(--file-tile-width) justify-between text-sm [--file-tile-image-size:3.625rem] [--file-tile-action-size:16px] [--file-tile-width:15rem] md:[--file-tile-width:20rem]" role="group" aria-label="learning-hub-main (5).zip"><div class="absolute inset-0 z-0 grid" data-default-action="true"><span class="grid" data-state="closed"><button type="button" class="interactive-bg-secondary border-token-interactive-border-secondary-default corner-superellipse/1.1 keyboard-focused:focus-ring grid rounded-xl border" aria-label="learning-hub-main (5).zip"></button></span></div><div class="pointer-events-none z-1 max-w-full min-w-0"><div class="w-full p-2"><div class="overflow flex flex-row items-center gap-2"><div class="corner-superellipse/1.1 relative h-10 w-10 shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-lg"><div class="inset-0 h-10 w-10 shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(146, 79, 247); display: none !important;"></div><div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg text-white" style="display: none !important;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="motion-safe:animate-spin text-token-text-secondary h-6 w-6"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-gvfid0kn.svg#4944fe" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></div><div class="flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg h-10 w-10 shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(146, 79, 247);"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true" class="h-5 w-5 text-white"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-sonic-bm18hwxp.svg#ab8f91" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></div></div><div class="overflow-hidden"><div class="truncate font-semibold">learning-hub-main (5).zip</div><div class="truncate text-token-text-secondary">Zip Archive</div></div></div></div></div><div class="z-1 flex items-start"></div></div></div><div class="flex flex-col gap-2 w-[80%]"></div><div class="user-message-bubble-color corner-superellipse/1.1 relative rounded-[18px] px-4 py-1.5 data-[multiline]:py-3 rounded-se-lg max-w-[var(--user-chat-width,70%)]" data-multiline=""><div class="whitespace-pre-wrap">This is the repo that I am using to develop the learning management system to support schools using the RootWork Framework.  The project has drifted quite a bit.  I need you to act as a Senior SaaS Engineer who has extensive experience in developing the most advanced and forward thinking LMSs for small to middle sized schools.  Analyze this repo and generate a phased plan to turn this repo into an industry exemplar for learning management systems that include agentic AI for teaching and learning in the k-12 environment including faculty and staff training. </div></div></div></div></div><div class="z-0 flex justify-end"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none touch:pointer-events-auto touch:opacity-100 duration-300 group-hover/turn-messages:delay-300 pointer-events-none opacity-0 motion-safe:transition-opacity group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:opacity-100 group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:opacity-100 has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:opacity-100" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-gvfid0kn.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span></button><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Edit message" aria-pressed="false" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-gvfid0kn.svg#6d87e1" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div><span class="sr-only"><br></span></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="request-WEB:7bee9ddd-eeaf-4d13-bbae-e0dc8b76c9b5-0" data-testid="conversation-turn-2" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div class="absolute flex h-8 w-3 origin-center items-center justify-center" style="opacity: 0; transform: scale(0);"><div class="bg-token-text-primary h-3 w-3 rounded-full"></div></div><div class="relative my-1 min-h-6"><div class="relative flex origin-top-left flex-col gap-2 overflow-x-clip rtl:origin-top-right" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><div class="relative w-full text-start"><div class="flex w-full flex-row items-start justify-between gap-4 text-start"><button class="flex min-w-0 shrink-1 items-center gap-0.5"><span class="font-medium w-full"><span class="flex items-center gap-1 truncate text-start align-middle text-token-text-secondary hover:text-token-text-primary dark:hover:text-token-text-primary dark:text-[var(--interactive-label-tertiary-default)]" style="opacity: 1;"><span class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1"><span class="min-w-0 truncate">Thought for 1m 45s</span></span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" data-rtl-flip="" class="icon-xs"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-gvfid0kn.svg#b140e7" fill="currentColor"></use></svg></span></span></button></div></div><div class="max-w-[calc(0.8*var(--thread-content-max-width,40rem))]"></div></div></div><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="f19141d9-b98c-48a0-abac-5590c61917d9" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-2-thinking"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word light markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="182">I unpacked the repo and you’re right: it has <strong data-start="45" data-end="78">multiple “centers of gravity”</strong> (tutoring/assessment + AI work-agent factory + book/content archive), which is why it feels like drift.</p>
<p data-start="184" data-end="649">That said, the codebase already contains <strong data-start="225" data-end="266">excellent “enterprise LMS primitives”</strong> you can build on (multi-tenancy, RBAC, audit logs, compliance endpoints, usage metering, curriculum ingestion/vector search, safety/anonymization, parent/educator surfaces). The fastest path to an industry-exemplar LMS is to <strong data-start="492" data-end="565">re-anchor the product around “School Ops + Learning Ops + Agentic AI”</strong> and treat the tutoring engine as one of several learning modalities inside the LMS.</p>
<hr data-start="651" data-end="654">
<h2 data-start="656" data-end="718">Critical issue to fix immediately (before any roadmap work)</h2>
<p data-start="719" data-end="839"><strong data-start="719" data-end="821">The repo contains a committed <code data-start="751" data-end="763">.env.local</code> with live-looking secrets (API keys / webhook secrets).</strong><br data-start="821" data-end="824">
Action (today):</p>
<ol data-start="840" data-end="1113">
<li data-start="840" data-end="934">
<p data-start="843" data-end="934"><strong data-start="843" data-end="899">Revoke/rotate every credential found in <code data-start="885" data-end="897">.env.local</code></strong> (Pinecone, Clerk, OpenAI, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="935" data-end="1036">
<p data-start="938" data-end="1036"><strong data-start="938" data-end="972">Purge secrets from git history</strong> (e.g., BFG Repo-Cleaner or <code data-start="1000" data-end="1017">git filter-repo</code>) and force-push.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1037" data-end="1113">
<p data-start="1040" data-end="1113">Add secret scanning + pre-commit hooks + CI checks to block this forever.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1115" data-end="1158">This is non-negotiable for a K–12 platform.</p>
<hr data-start="1160" data-end="1163">
<h2 data-start="1165" data-end="1222">What the repo is <em data-start="1185" data-end="1194">already</em> good at (keep and leverage)</h2>
<p data-start="1223" data-end="1275">These are “unusually strong” foundations for an LMS:</p>
<ul data-start="1276" data-end="1863">
<li data-start="1276" data-end="1364">
<p data-start="1278" data-end="1364"><strong data-start="1278" data-end="1299">Multi-tenant SaaS</strong>: <code data-start="1301" data-end="1309">Tenant</code>, <code data-start="1311" data-end="1319">School</code>, <code data-start="1321" data-end="1328">Class</code>, <code data-start="1330" data-end="1336">User</code> + subscription scaffolding.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1365" data-end="1420">
<p data-start="1367" data-end="1420"><strong data-start="1367" data-end="1390">RBAC + auditability</strong>: RBAC utilities + <code data-start="1409" data-end="1419">AuditLog</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1421" data-end="1506">
<p data-start="1423" data-end="1506"><strong data-start="1423" data-end="1445">Compliance posture</strong>: consent/data-rights/data-retention endpoints already exist.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1507" data-end="1650">
<p data-start="1509" data-end="1650"><strong data-start="1509" data-end="1537">Learning science engines</strong>: IRT (<code data-start="1544" data-end="1561">ItemCalibration</code>, <code data-start="1563" data-end="1579">StudentAbility</code>), spaced repetition (<code data-start="1601" data-end="1617">ReviewSchedule</code>), assessments + progress models.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1651" data-end="1863">
<p data-start="1653" data-end="1863"><strong data-start="1653" data-end="1676">Agentic AI plumbing</strong>: <code data-start="1678" data-end="1689">/api/chat</code> includes curriculum retrieval (vector search), anonymization, usage limits, dysregulation detection + intervention formatting, and evaluation hooks (NVC quality evaluation).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1865" data-end="1916">So you’re not “starting over”—you’re <strong data-start="1902" data-end="1915">reframing</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="1918" data-end="1921">
<h2 data-start="1923" data-end="1966">The drift (what’s pulling it off-course)</h2>
<ul data-start="1967" data-end="2389">
<li data-start="1967" data-end="2075">
<p data-start="1969" data-end="2075"><strong data-start="1969" data-end="1995">Repo identity mismatch</strong>: package name + schema say “tutoring platform,” README says “AI agent factory.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2076" data-end="2189">
<p data-start="2078" data-end="2189"><strong data-start="2078" data-end="2111">Content warehouse in the repo</strong>: many book chapters / curriculum content folders live alongside the SaaS app.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2190" data-end="2389">
<p data-start="2192" data-end="2389"><strong data-start="2192" data-end="2218">Missing LMS core loops</strong>: assignments → submissions → grading → feedback → gradebook → transcripts; course authoring; PD micro-credentials; messaging; calendars; integrations (OneRoster/LTI/SSO).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2391" data-end="2394">
<h1 data-start="2396" data-end="2461">Phased plan to turn this into an industry-exemplar RootWork LMS</h1>
<h2 data-start="2463" data-end="2506">Phase 0 — Re-anchor + harden (1–2 weeks)</h2>
<p data-start="2507" data-end="2581"><strong data-start="2507" data-end="2516">Goal:</strong> Make the platform safe, coherent, and buildable—no new features.</p>
<p data-start="2583" data-end="2595">Deliverables</p>
<ul data-start="2596" data-end="3551">
<li data-start="2596" data-end="2772">
<p data-start="2598" data-end="2620"><strong data-start="2598" data-end="2620">Security hardening</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2623" data-end="2772">
<li data-start="2623" data-end="2655">
<p data-start="2625" data-end="2655">rotate + purge secrets (above)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2658" data-end="2712">
<p data-start="2660" data-end="2712">enable CI secret scanning, dependency scanning, SAST</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2715" data-end="2772">
<p data-start="2717" data-end="2772">tighten logging to avoid accidental student PII leakage</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2773" data-end="2955">
<p data-start="2775" data-end="2810"><strong data-start="2775" data-end="2810">Product “source of truth” reset</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2813" data-end="2955">
<li data-start="2813" data-end="2868">
<p data-start="2815" data-end="2868">Replace README with <strong data-start="2835" data-end="2868">RootWork LMS vision + modules</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start="2871" data-end="2955">
<p data-start="2873" data-end="2955">Add <code data-start="2877" data-end="2893">/docs/product/</code> with: roles, primary flows, data classification, safety rules</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2956" data-end="3162">
<p data-start="2958" data-end="2982"><strong data-start="2958" data-end="2982">Repo re-organization</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2985" data-end="3162">
<li data-start="2985" data-end="3115">
<p data-start="2987" data-end="3115">Move the book/content directories into a separate <code data-start="3037" data-end="3047">content/</code> repo <strong data-start="3053" data-end="3059">or</strong> mount them via storage (S3/R2/GCS) + ingestion pipeline</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3118" data-end="3162">
<p data-start="3120" data-end="3162">Keep this repo as <strong data-start="3138" data-end="3162">the SaaS application</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="3163" data-end="3391">
<p data-start="3165" data-end="3186"><strong data-start="3165" data-end="3186">Role-separated UI</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3189" data-end="3391">
<li data-start="3189" data-end="3391">
<p data-start="3191" data-end="3295">Your app already has educator/parent/admin routes, but the overall experience needs strict role routing:</p>
<ul data-start="3300" data-end="3391">
<li data-start="3300" data-end="3391">
<p data-start="3302" data-end="3391"><code data-start="3302" data-end="3312">/student</code>, <code data-start="3314" data-end="3323">/parent</code>, <code data-start="3325" data-end="3336">/educator</code>, <code data-start="3338" data-end="3353">/school-admin</code>, <code data-start="3355" data-end="3372">/district-admin</code>, <code data-start="3374" data-end="3391">/platform-admin</code></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="3392" data-end="3551">
<p data-start="3394" data-end="3418"><strong data-start="3394" data-end="3418">Operational baseline</strong></p>
<ul data-start="3421" data-end="3551">
<li data-start="3421" data-end="3487">
<p data-start="3423" data-end="3487">“golden path” e2e tests for sign-in + student/educator dashboard</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3490" data-end="3551">
<p data-start="3492" data-end="3551">health checks, metrics endpoints wired to deployment checks</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3553" data-end="3571">Definition of Done</p>
<ul data-start="3572" data-end="3655">
<li data-start="3572" data-end="3655">
<p data-start="3574" data-end="3655">Clean build, clean deploy, clean secrets posture, role-based navigation enforced.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="3657" data-end="3660">
<h2 data-start="3662" data-end="3721">Phase 1 — LMS Core (School Ops + Course Ops) (3–6 weeks)</h2>
<p data-start="3722" data-end="3782"><strong data-start="3722" data-end="3731">Goal:</strong> Become a real LMS (not just tutoring/assessments).</p>
<p data-start="3784" data-end="3817">Add/expand domain models (Prisma)</p>
<ul data-start="3818" data-end="4371">
<li data-start="3818" data-end="3849">
<p data-start="3820" data-end="3849"><code data-start="3820" data-end="3828">Course</code> (district catalog)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3850" data-end="3897">
<p data-start="3852" data-end="3897"><code data-start="3852" data-end="3861">Section</code> (offering by term/school/teacher)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3898" data-end="3936">
<p data-start="3900" data-end="3936"><code data-start="3900" data-end="3906">Term</code> (grading periods/semesters)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3937" data-end="3990">
<p data-start="3939" data-end="3990"><code data-start="3939" data-end="3951">Enrollment</code> (student↔section; parent visibility)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3991" data-end="4049">
<p data-start="3993" data-end="4049"><code data-start="3993" data-end="4005">Assignment</code> (type, rubric, due dates, accommodations)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4050" data-end="4105">
<p data-start="4052" data-end="4105"><code data-start="4052" data-end="4064">Submission</code> (files, links, text, revision history)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4106" data-end="4154">
<p data-start="4108" data-end="4154"><code data-start="4108" data-end="4115">Grade</code> (rubric scoring + standards scoring)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4155" data-end="4208">
<p data-start="4157" data-end="4208"><code data-start="4157" data-end="4176">GradebookSnapshot</code> (report cards / final grades)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4209" data-end="4252">
<p data-start="4211" data-end="4252"><code data-start="4211" data-end="4221">Resource</code> (teacher-uploaded materials)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4253" data-end="4317">
<p data-start="4255" data-end="4317"><code data-start="4255" data-end="4269">Announcement</code> + <code data-start="4272" data-end="4287">MessageThread</code> (school/home communication)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4318" data-end="4371">
<p data-start="4320" data-end="4371"><code data-start="4320" data-end="4332">Attendance</code> (optional early, but schools will ask)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4373" data-end="4388">Core UI modules</p>
<ul data-start="4389" data-end="4630">
<li data-start="4389" data-end="4458">
<p data-start="4391" data-end="4458">Teacher: course home → roster → assignments → gradebook → messaging</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4459" data-end="4516">
<p data-start="4461" data-end="4516">Student: courses → assignments → submissions → feedback</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4517" data-end="4574">
<p data-start="4519" data-end="4574">Parent: child courses → missing work → teacher messages</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4575" data-end="4630">
<p data-start="4577" data-end="4630">Admin: terms, sections, rostering, compliance reports</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="4632" data-end="4635">DoD</p>
<ul data-start="4636" data-end="4704">
<li data-start="4636" data-end="4704">
<p data-start="4638" data-end="4704">A teacher can run a class end-to-end without leaving the platform.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="4706" data-end="4709">
<h2 data-start="4711" data-end="4782">Phase 2 — RootWork Learning Experience (2–5 weeks, overlaps Phase 1)</h2>
<p data-start="4783" data-end="4842"><strong data-start="4783" data-end="4792">Goal:</strong> Make it <em data-start="4801" data-end="4822">distinctly RootWork</em>, not a generic LMS.</p>
<p data-start="4844" data-end="4878">Build “RootWork as first-class UX”</p>
<ul data-start="4879" data-end="5388">
<li data-start="4879" data-end="5156">
<p data-start="4881" data-end="4974"><strong data-start="4881" data-end="4893">5R cycle</strong> surfaces already exist (<code data-start="4918" data-end="4930">FiveRPhase</code>): turn them into a <strong data-start="4950" data-end="4973">daily learning flow</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="4977" data-end="5156">
<li data-start="4977" data-end="5156">
<p data-start="4979" data-end="5156">ROOT (warmup/diagnostic) → REGULATE (check-in + strategies) → REFLECT (journal/exit ticket) → RESTORE (spaced review / make-up work) → RECONNECT (community/collaboration prompt)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="5157" data-end="5388">
<p data-start="5159" data-end="5194"><strong data-start="5159" data-end="5194">Regulation-informed instruction</strong></p>
<ul data-start="5197" data-end="5388">
<li data-start="5197" data-end="5388">
<p data-start="5199" data-end="5256">You already detect dysregulation in chat—connect that to:</p>
<ul data-start="5261" data-end="5388">
<li data-start="5261" data-end="5297">
<p data-start="5263" data-end="5297">“suggested supports” for educators</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5302" data-end="5333">
<p data-start="5304" data-end="5333">student self-regulation tools</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5338" data-end="5388">
<p data-start="5340" data-end="5388">MTSS-style flags (without stigmatizing language)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5390" data-end="5402">Deliverables</p>
<ul data-start="5403" data-end="5595">
<li data-start="5403" data-end="5460">
<p data-start="5405" data-end="5460">RootWork daily session template (teacher can assign it)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5461" data-end="5595">
<p data-start="5463" data-end="5509">Student “learning session player” that blends:</p>
<ul data-start="5512" data-end="5595">
<li data-start="5512" data-end="5529">
<p data-start="5514" data-end="5529">teacher content</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5532" data-end="5545">
<p data-start="5534" data-end="5545">assessments</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5548" data-end="5570">
<p data-start="5550" data-end="5570">AI-assisted tutoring</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5573" data-end="5595">
<p data-start="5575" data-end="5595">reflection artifacts</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="5597" data-end="5600">DoD</p>
<ul data-start="5601" data-end="5678">
<li data-start="5601" data-end="5678">
<p data-start="5603" data-end="5678">RootWork is not a “theme”—it’s a functional operating model inside the LMS.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="5680" data-end="5683">
<h2 data-start="5685" data-end="5748">Phase 3 — Agentic AI as an embedded “co-teacher” (4–8 weeks)</h2>
<p data-start="5749" data-end="5835"><strong data-start="5749" data-end="5758">Goal:</strong> Best-in-class agentic AI for K–12 with safety, auditability, and usefulness.</p>
<h3 data-start="5837" data-end="5888">3A. Teacher Copilot (high leverage, safest ROI)</h3>
<ul data-start="5889" data-end="6210">
<li data-start="5889" data-end="6078">
<p data-start="5891" data-end="5930">Lesson/assignment generator aligned to:</p>
<ul data-start="5933" data-end="6078">
<li data-start="5933" data-end="5964">
<p data-start="5935" data-end="5964">standards + course objectives</p>
</li>
<li data-start="5967" data-end="6021">
<p data-start="5969" data-end="6021">accommodations/IEP supports (carefully permissioned)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6024" data-end="6078">
<p data-start="6026" data-end="6078">differentiation (tiered tasks, scaffolds, exemplars)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="6079" data-end="6124">
<p data-start="6081" data-end="6124">Auto-rubric drafting + feedback suggestions</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6125" data-end="6210">
<p data-start="6127" data-end="6210">“What happened in class?” summaries from allowed artifacts (no covert surveillance)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="6212" data-end="6258">3B. Student Tutor (your existing strength)</h3>
<ul data-start="6259" data-end="6486">
<li data-start="6259" data-end="6486">
<p data-start="6261" data-end="6292">Keep <code data-start="6266" data-end="6277">/api/chat</code> but formalize:</p>
<ul data-start="6295" data-end="6486">
<li data-start="6295" data-end="6354">
<p data-start="6297" data-end="6354"><strong data-start="6297" data-end="6316">tool boundaries</strong> (what it may access; what it may not)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6357" data-end="6412">
<p data-start="6359" data-end="6412"><strong data-start="6359" data-end="6383">citation requirement</strong> for curriculum-based answers</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6415" data-end="6460">
<p data-start="6417" data-end="6460"><strong data-start="6417" data-end="6432">hint ladder</strong> + “don’t just give answers”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6463" data-end="6486">
<p data-start="6465" data-end="6486">safe refusal patterns</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="6488" data-end="6536">3C. Staff Training Agents (faculty/staff PD)</h3>
<ul data-start="6537" data-end="6732">
<li data-start="6537" data-end="6732">
<p data-start="6539" data-end="6577">PD module uses the same agentic layer:</p>
<ul data-start="6580" data-end="6732">
<li data-start="6580" data-end="6635">
<p data-start="6582" data-end="6635">training courses, scenario practice, knowledge checks</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6638" data-end="6666">
<p data-start="6640" data-end="6666">micro-credentials / badges</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6669" data-end="6732">
<p data-start="6671" data-end="6732">district playbooks + policy Q&amp;A (RAG from approved docs only)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6734" data-end="6765">Safety &amp; governance (must-have)</p>
<ul data-start="6766" data-end="7108">
<li data-start="6766" data-end="6821">
<p data-start="6768" data-end="6821">Data minimization + anonymization enforced by default</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6822" data-end="6925">
<p data-start="6824" data-end="6865">AI usage ledger already exists—extend to:</p>
<ul data-start="6868" data-end="6925">
<li data-start="6868" data-end="6925">
<p data-start="6870" data-end="6925">per-user, per-student, per-feature billing + guardrails</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="6926" data-end="7108">
<p data-start="6928" data-end="6947">Evaluation harness:</p>
<ul data-start="6950" data-end="7108">
<li data-start="6950" data-end="7019">
<p data-start="6952" data-end="7019">rubric-based safety/quality checks (your NVC evaluation is a start)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7022" data-end="7108">
<p data-start="7024" data-end="7108">red-team prompts (self-harm, violence, hate, sexual content, personal data requests)</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="7110" data-end="7113">DoD</p>
<ul data-start="7114" data-end="7193">
<li data-start="7114" data-end="7193">
<p data-start="7116" data-end="7193">AI is not a chat widget. It is a permissioned, audited, role-specific system.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="7195" data-end="7198">
<h2 data-start="7200" data-end="7262">Phase 4 — Analytics, MTSS support, and evidence (4–8 weeks)</h2>
<p data-start="7263" data-end="7328"><strong data-start="7263" data-end="7272">Goal:</strong> The platform proves impact and supports administrators.</p>
<p data-start="7330" data-end="7340">Dashboards</p>
<ul data-start="7341" data-end="7600">
<li data-start="7341" data-end="7383">
<p data-start="7343" data-end="7383">Student mastery (standards + objectives)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7384" data-end="7422">
<p data-start="7386" data-end="7422">Assignment completion + missing work</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7423" data-end="7479">
<p data-start="7425" data-end="7479">Growth over time (use your assessment/progress models)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7480" data-end="7539">
<p data-start="7482" data-end="7539">Regulation trend signals (aggregated, privacy-protecting)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7540" data-end="7600">
<p data-start="7542" data-end="7600">Teacher effectiveness supports: “where students are stuck”</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="7602" data-end="7634">Reporting outputs schools demand</p>
<ul data-start="7635" data-end="7749">
<li data-start="7635" data-end="7671">
<p data-start="7637" data-end="7671">progress reports, parent summaries</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7672" data-end="7694">
<p data-start="7674" data-end="7694">exportable gradebook</p>
</li>
<li data-start="7695" data-end="7749">
<p data-start="7697" data-end="7749">compliance reports (consent, retention, access logs)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="7751" data-end="7754">DoD</p>
<ul data-start="7755" data-end="7830">
<li data-start="7755" data-end="7830">
<p data-start="7757" data-end="7830">Admins can run the school from the platform; teachers can prove learning.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="7832" data-end="7835">
<h2 data-start="7837" data-end="7908">Phase 5 — Integrations that make it “real school ready” (6–12 weeks)</h2>
<p data-start="7909" data-end="7954"><strong data-start="7909" data-end="7918">Goal:</strong> Plug into existing K–12 ecosystems.</p>
<p data-start="7956" data-end="7993">Priority integrations (in this order)</p>
<ol data-start="7994" data-end="8343">
<li data-start="7994" data-end="8063">
<p data-start="7997" data-end="8063"><strong data-start="7997" data-end="8021">Roster import/export</strong> (OneRoster CSV first, then OneRoster API)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8064" data-end="8127">
<p data-start="8067" data-end="8127"><strong data-start="8067" data-end="8074">SSO</strong> (Clever/ClassLink optional depending on your target)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8128" data-end="8207">
<p data-start="8131" data-end="8207"><strong data-start="8131" data-end="8151">Google/Microsoft</strong> file + calendar integration (attachments + submissions)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8208" data-end="8274">
<p data-start="8211" data-end="8274"><strong data-start="8211" data-end="8222">LTI 1.3</strong> (to be “tool-provider” and/or embed external tools)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8275" data-end="8343">
<p data-start="8278" data-end="8343"><strong data-start="8278" data-end="8293">SIS exports</strong> for transcripts/records (state/district specific)</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="8345" data-end="8348">DoD</p>
<ul data-start="8349" data-end="8403">
<li data-start="8349" data-end="8403">
<p data-start="8351" data-end="8403">A school can adopt without a painful data migration.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="8405" data-end="8408">
<h2 data-start="8410" data-end="8460">Phase 6 — Premium production standard (ongoing)</h2>
<p data-start="8461" data-end="8501"><strong data-start="8461" data-end="8470">Goal:</strong> “Audit-ready, district-ready.”</p>
<ul data-start="8503" data-end="8807">
<li data-start="8503" data-end="8558">
<p data-start="8505" data-end="8558">SLOs, load tests (you already have load test scripts)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8559" data-end="8621">
<p data-start="8561" data-end="8621">Observability (Sentry/Datadog already in deps—finish wiring)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8622" data-end="8679">
<p data-start="8624" data-end="8679">Backups, retention policies, incident response runbooks</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8680" data-end="8753">
<p data-start="8682" data-end="8753">Accessibility conformance (playwright a11y tests exist—expand coverage)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8754" data-end="8807">
<p data-start="8756" data-end="8807">SOC2-style controls (even if you don’t certify yet)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="8809" data-end="8812">
<h1 data-start="8814" data-end="8871">Recommended “North Star” module map (industry exemplar)</h1>
<ol data-start="8872" data-end="9338">
<li data-start="8872" data-end="8938">
<p data-start="8875" data-end="8938"><strong data-start="8875" data-end="8887">Core LMS</strong> (courses/sections/assignments/gradebook/messaging)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="8939" data-end="9001">
<p data-start="8942" data-end="9001"><strong data-start="8942" data-end="8969">RootWork Daily Learning</strong> (5R session player + artifacts)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9002" data-end="9068">
<p data-start="9005" data-end="9068"><strong data-start="9005" data-end="9029">Assessment &amp; Mastery</strong> (IRT + standards mastery + SRS review)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9069" data-end="9142">
<p data-start="9072" data-end="9142"><strong data-start="9072" data-end="9092">Agentic AI Layer</strong> (teacher copilot + student tutor + staff trainer)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9143" data-end="9205">
<p data-start="9146" data-end="9205"><strong data-start="9146" data-end="9175">Analytics &amp; MTSS supports</strong> (privacy-protecting insights)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9206" data-end="9281">
<p data-start="9209" data-end="9281"><strong data-start="9209" data-end="9236">Compliance &amp; Governance</strong> (consent, retention, access logs, AI ledger)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9282" data-end="9338">
<p data-start="9285" data-end="9338"><strong data-start="9285" data-end="9301">Integrations</strong> (rostering, SSO, LTI, cloud storage)</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="9340" data-end="9343">
<h2 data-start="9345" data-end="9386">Your best next move (highest leverage)</h2>
<p data-start="9387" data-end="9587">If you do only one thing next: <strong data-start="9418" data-end="9462">Phase 0 + Phase 1 “LMS Core thin slice.”</strong><br data-start="9462" data-end="9465">
Meaning: one school → one term → one teacher → one section → one assignment → one submission → one grade → parent sees it.</p>
<p data-start="9589" data-end="9670">That thin slice becomes the backbone that your <strong data-start="9636" data-end="9650">agentic AI</strong> plugs into cleanly.</p>
<hr data-start="9672" data-end="9675">
<p data-start="9677" data-end="9719">If you want, I can follow up by producing:</p>
<ul data-start="9720" data-end="9971" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">
<li data-start="9720" data-end="9824">
<p data-start="9722" data-end="9824">a <strong data-start="9724" data-end="9758">Phase 0–2 GitHub Issue backlog</strong> with DoD + acceptance criteria + exact files/routes to touch, and</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9825" data-end="9971" data-is-last-node="">
<p data-start="9827" data-end="9971" data-is-last-node="">a <strong data-start="9829" data-end="9857">Prisma schema patch plan</strong> (models + migrations) that cleanly extends what you already have without breaking the tutoring/assessment engine.</p>
</li>
