<h1 data-start="587" data-end="639">✅ MASTER PROMPT FOR CODEX (WITH BRAND INTEGRATION)</h1>
<pre class="overflow-visible! px-0!" data-start="641" data-end="6485"><div class="contain-inline-size rounded-2xl corner-superellipse/1.1 relative bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary"><div class="flex items-center text-token-text-secondary px-4 py-2 text-xs font-sans justify-between h-9 bg-token-sidebar-surface-primary select-none rounded-t-2xl corner-t-superellipse/1.1">text</div><div class="sticky top-[calc(var(--sticky-padding-top)+9*var(--spacing))]"><div class="absolute end-0 bottom-0 flex h-9 items-center pe-2"><div class="bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary text-token-text-secondary flex items-center gap-4 rounded-sm px-2 font-sans text-xs"><button class="flex gap-1 items-center select-none py-1" aria-label="Copy"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" class="icon-sm"><use href="/cdn/assets/sprites-core-gvfid0kn.svg#ce3544" fill="currentColor"></use></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-text"><span><span>You are Codex acting as:

- Senior SaaS Engineer
- K–12 Security Lead
- Brand Systems Architect
- LMS Platform Architect

Repository: learning-hub (RootWork Framework LMS)

MISSION
Thoroughly scrub, reposition, and rebrand this repository as the definitive
RootWork Learning Hub (RootWork LMS), integrating:

• Security remediation (secrets scrub + prevention)
• Structural realignment (LMS-first architecture)
• Agentic AI governance
• Role-based routing hardening
• AND full RootWork branding integration:
  - RWFW logo
  - 5R icons (Root, Regulate, Reflect, Restore, Reconnect)
  - Color system
  - Typography references
  - Asset normalization
  - UI and docs embedding

This must result in a clean, audit-ready, production-ready, brand-consistent SaaS platform.

NON-NEGOTIABLES (K–12 + Brand Integrity)
1. Never expose secrets.
2. Treat student data as protected.
3. Preserve design consistency.
4. Do NOT fabricate logos or icons — locate existing RWFW assets in the repo.
5. Normalize asset paths and formats without altering original art integrity.
6. Ensure dark-mode and light-mode compatibility for logos.
7. Produce changes as structured PRs with test plans.

--------------------------------------------
STEP 1 — LOCATE ROOTWORK BRAND ASSETS
--------------------------------------------

Search the entire repo for:

- RWFW logo files
- RootWork logo files
- 5R icons (Root, Regulate, Reflect, Restore, Reconnect)
- SVG, PNG, AI, EPS, or JPG variants
- Any Canva export artifacts
- Any color palette definitions

If multiple versions exist:
- Choose the highest-resolution or vector (SVG preferred)
- Standardize under:

  /public/brand/
      rwfw-logo.svg
      rwfw-logo-dark.svg (if needed)
      5r-root.svg
      5r-regulate.svg
      5r-reflect.svg
      5r-restore.svg
      5r-reconnect.svg
      favicon.svg

If icons are only PNG:
- Preserve originals
- Convert to optimized SVG only if clean vector source exists
- Do NOT auto-trace raster files

Document findings in:
docs/BRAND_AUDIT.md

--------------------------------------------
STEP 2 — CREATE ROOTWORK BRAND SYSTEM
--------------------------------------------

Create:

docs/BRAND_SYSTEM.md

Include:

• Logo usage guidelines
• Clear space rules
• Light/dark mode handling
• Official color palette (extract from logo if not defined)
• Icon meaning definitions:

  ROOT — diagnostic grounding
  REGULATE — nervous system stabilization
  REFLECT — metacognition
  RESTORE — repair and reinforcement
  RECONNECT — collaboration/community

• Approved UI placements
• Minimum size requirements
• Do NOT stretch or recolor policy

--------------------------------------------
STEP 3 — EMBED BRANDING THROUGHOUT THE PLATFORM
--------------------------------------------

UI INTEGRATION TASKS

1. Replace generic or placeholder logos with RWFW logo.
2. Update navigation header with RWFW logo.
3. Add 5R icon strip to:
   - Student dashboard
   - Teacher dashboard
   - RootWork session flow
4. Use icons in:
   - 5R daily learning flow UI
   - AI hint ladder UI
   - Staff training module
5. Add favicon using RWFW icon.

Ensure:
- SVG imported properly
- No broken asset references
- Accessible alt text added
- aria-labels included
- Icons do not distort layout

--------------------------------------------
STEP 4 — BRAND-INFORMED README &amp; DOCS
--------------------------------------------

Update:

README.md

Add:
- Embedded RWFW logo at top
- 5R icon strip graphic
- Section headers using icons
- Visual module map

Update CLAUDE.md to include brand integrity section:

## Brand Integrity Rules
- Always use official RWFW logo
- Never generate alternate logos
- Use 5R icons only for their defined phases
- Do not recolor brand assets without approval

--------------------------------------------
STEP 5 — VISUAL CONSISTENCY CHECK
--------------------------------------------

Audit:
- All dashboards
- Login pages
- Public landing page
- Parent view
- Admin view

Ensure:
- Consistent spacing
- Logo placement uniform
- Icon alignment clean
- Colors consistent with palette
- No mixed branding (e.g., tutoring platform leftovers)

--------------------------------------------
STEP 6 — FOLDER RESTRUCTURE FOR BRAND CLARITY
--------------------------------------------

Create:

/public/brand
/components/brand

Move:
- All reusable brand components to components/brand

Create:
BrandLogo.tsx
FiveRIcon.tsx (generic wrapper)
FiveRStrip.tsx

Ensure:
- Icons centrally imported
- No duplicated SVG inline copies scattered across app

--------------------------------------------
STEP 7 — CREATE PR SERIES (UPDATED WITH BRANDING)
--------------------------------------------

PR0: security/secrets-scrub-and-history-rewrite
PR1: docs/reposition-rootwork-lms
PR2: brand/asset-standardization-and-brand-system
